	r := []rune(s)
	for i, j := 0, len(r)-1; i < j; i, j = i+1, j-1 {
		r[i], r[j] = r[j], r[i]
	}
	return string(r)
}
```

**Caveat:** converting to `[]rune` replaces invalid bytes with `U+FFFD` (�), so the output may differ from a true reversal.

## Limitation: Grapheme Clusters

Both versions reverse **code points**, not user-perceived characters. Combining sequences will be split apart:

```go
Reverse("e\u0301")  // "é" written as e + combining acute accent
// -> "\u0301e"     // the accent now attaches to the wrong character
```

Emoji built from several code points (such as 👨‍👩‍👧 or flag emoji) are affected the same way. For grapheme-aware reversal, use a segmentation library like [`github.com/rivo/uniseg`](https://github.com/rivo/uniseg):

```go
